    "updated_at": "2021-01-31T16:19:54Z",
    "body": "Hello @LitoMore,\r\n\r\nthank you very much for pointing that out. We currently have a lot of issues in regards to extended configuration.\r\n\r\nIn the meantime, you could remove the `in` from the `username` and `hostname` module and place it in the `directory` module and place an `on` in front of the `hostname` module (if you always display the `username` when you display the `hostname` and the `directory` module is directly behind the `hostname` module) like:\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[hostname]\r\nformat = \" on [$hostname]($style)\"\r\n\r\n[directory]\r\nformat = \" in [$path]($style)[$read_only]($read_only_style) \"\r\n\r\n[username]\r\nformat = \"[$user]($style)\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nTake care\r\nMick\r\n\r\nPS: I would call it an _enhancement_ and not a _bug_, if that is ok with you.",
